sections.text:
(1) Whoever threatens another with any injury to his person, reputation or property, or to the person or reputation or property of any one in whom that person is interested, with intent to cause alarm to that person, or to cause that person to do any act which he is not legally bound to do, or to omit to do any act which that person is legally entitled to do, as the means of avoiding the execution of such threat, commits criminal intimidation.
(2) Whoever commits the offence of criminal intimidation shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to two years, or with fine, or with both;
and if the threat is to cause death or grievous hurt, or to cause the destruction of any property by fire, shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to seven years, or with fine, or with both.
